# SQL injection: a query sink (execute/query/prepare) whose SQL string is built
# dynamically and contains SELECT. Promoted from the learn loop
# (LEARNED-1789868567-4). Anchored on the sink + the SQL keyword. Target narrowed
# to code extensions on promotion.
id: KEUR-SQLI-001
ilities: [integrity]
maturity: 2
title: Potential SQL injection via dynamically built query
category: sqli
severity: critical
engine: pattern
action: block
target:
  extensions: .js .php .rb .py .ts .go .java
patterns:
  - regex: (?i)\b(?:execute|query|prepare)\s*\(\s*(?:"[^"]*\bselect\b[^"]*"|'[^']*\bselect\b[^']*')\s*[%+.]
    message: A SQL query sink is called with a SELECT string that is then combined with other values (%, +, ., format args) — potential SQL injection (CWE-89). Use parameterised queries / prepared statements with bound parameters.
confidence: 0.8
fix: Use parameterised queries or an ORM with bound parameters; never concatenate untrusted input into SQL.
